<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dezhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dezhou is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a>. In 1417 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paduka-batara">Paduka Batara</a>, one of the rulers of Sulu who led a mission to the Ming court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a>, died there on his journey home and was buried with imperial honours. His tomb still stands, and descendants of his family who stayed behind have lived in Dezhou since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dezhou.jpg" alt="Dezhou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suginami · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dezhou_Xinhu_view_from_Diecuishan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
